{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022902-consecrated-items","id":1022902,"title":"Consecrated items","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T12:39:17-08:00","id":1022902,"title":"Consecrated items","content":"Ok so about consecrated items with prime 1, can they like be robbed from you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:09:42-08:00","id":1022914,"title":"","content":"As everything in Mage, it depends. But if you're talking just about Prime, yes, they most probably can.<br /> <br /> The questions are: what Consecrate means for the creator? What effects where mechanically used to achieve the result? What it all means to the robber? Once the thing leaves the hands of a Mage to go to other, you start to thread the murky waters of interacting Paradigms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:10:44-08:00","id":1022916,"title":"","content":"I'd say yes they can, but you would notice the attempt without difficulty, just as you'd notice someone trying to hold your hand.<br /> <br /> It would also be more difficult to tear it off you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:26:03-08:00","id":1022950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022902-consecrated-items?p=1022914#post1022914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As everything in Mage, it depends. But if you're talking just about Prime, yes, they most probably can.<br /> <br /> The questions are: what Consecrate means for the creator? What effects where mechanically used to achieve the result? What it all means to the robber? Once the thing leaves the hands of a Mage to go to other, you start to thread the murky waters of interacting Paradigms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see Cultists of Ecstasy being pretty relaxed about Consecrated items. All they have to do after losing one is snort a couple of fat lines over another necklace...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T16:34:08-08:00","id":1023024,"title":"","content":"The big thing to remember is that if consecrated items fall into the wrong hands, those wrong hands have a -3 difficulty of using magick against you because they essentially posses something that's more directly connected to you than a long-time personal item - the item is directly infused with the Mage's resonance, if not pattern. It can also be argued that the item also can be used to make creating a correspondence link to you minimal-successes-dead-easy.<br /> <br /> You don't want to lose your consecreated items if you don't have a quick, sure way of retrieval.<br /> Even if the Mage in question has no known enemies that are directly after them, it's like losing metaphysical keys to yourself, and you don't know if and when they suddenly turn into a world of sudden pain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:05:46-08:00","id":1023032,"title":"","content":"Of course consecrated items can be stolen. Unless they're literally fused to your body (like when you're shapeshifting), consecrated items are items. It's not like they're glued to you. Granted, they are easy to teleport back to you (high level of connection = low success threshold), assuming you have Correspondence. Not every Mage invests in that Sphere, as there are reasons to consecrate items that don't involve it (the aforementioned shapeshifting, or Umbral travel).<br /> <br /> Even if you have the ability to take an item back (which might require Corr 3 in the case of larger items), a thief could attempt to stymie your attempts to do so with Correspondence wards of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}